<title>UK: Zeneca leads drug rally after U.S. elections.</title>
<headline>Zeneca leads drug rally after U.S. elections.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Britain's major pharmaceutical concerns jumped on Wednesday amid relief that Republicans retained control of the U.S. Congress, traders said.</p>
<p>A Republican majority in both houses of the Congress means it will be more difficult for the White House to push through health care reforms, they said.</p>
<p>By 0837 GMT, shares in Zeneca Group climbed 14p to 1641-1/2p. Shares in Glaxo Wellcome added 10p to 971p, while SmithKline Beecham rose 11-1/2p to 764-1/2p.  </p>
<p>&quot;There were worries that if the Democrats took control of the Congress, then health care reforms would go through and put the squeeze on (profit) margins,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>-- Debra Sherman, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
